  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What the engine guarantees",
      "items": [
        "Typed run inputs are checked before a run is created",
        "Secrets are resolved per step and never stored in the runbook",
        "Steps cannot reach private addresses on a shared server",
        "Every step outcome is appended to a hash-chained audit log"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Reading this diagram",
      "items": [
        "Webhooks and cron are separate entry points, drawn as one node",
        "API v1, webhooks and cron call the engine directly",
        "The editor view listens on the socket; the sessions board polls /api/runs"
      ]
    }
